WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:00.705
Hey, everyone,

2
00:00:00.705 --> 00:00:02.395
I'm Chase with
the Basecamp team,

3
00:00:02.395 --> 00:00:04.650
I'm here show you a couple
of different advanced tips

4
00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:07.124
and tricks to help you get
the most out of Basecamp,

5
00:00:07.124 --> 00:00:09.290
So we're going to start on
the Projects screen here,

6
00:00:09.290 --> 00:00:10.956
and a lot of times
you want to customize

7
00:00:10.956 --> 00:00:13.680
the way that looks, how it
feels, just to make things

8
00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:14.910
a little easier to get into,

9
00:00:14.910 --> 00:00:16.880
So we've got three
different options here,

10
00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:18.910
The first one is
a Cards view that

11
00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:22.380
gives us all the projects
in a card just like this,

12
00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:24.010
The third one here
is a List view,

13
00:00:24.010 --> 00:00:25.690
It's all your projects
alphabetically

14
00:00:25.690 --> 00:00:27.940
just like a list like
you would print out,

15
00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:30.840
and the middle one here
gives us a mix of those two,

16
00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:33.670
Now, one of the ways that
I like to separate out

17
00:00:33.670 --> 00:00:36.730
the projects that I'm working
on is by starring them,

18
00:00:36.730 --> 00:00:40.990
So for instance, if I'm working
on this Newsroom project--

19
00:00:40.990 --> 00:00:42.640
I'm just going to
click this star--

20
00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:45.100
and you can see it appears
as a card project up here

21
00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:46.270
at the top,

22
00:00:46.270 --> 00:00:49.440
We'll do a couple other ones
like this Help Page Redesign

23
00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:52.830
one, and then maybe these
Class Questions right here,

24
00:00:52.830 --> 00:00:55.610
So then I'll bring these
up to the top as cards,

25
00:00:55.610 --> 00:00:57.730
If I want to remove any
of them, super simple,

26
00:00:57.730 --> 00:01:01.909
We'll just unstar the
project like that,

27
00:01:01.909 --> 00:01:03.950
and we can always bring
those back up if we want,

28
00:01:03.950 --> 00:01:06.150
Now, these are always going
to appear in the order

29
00:01:06.150 --> 00:01:09.240
that you star them in, so if
I star the Class Questions

30
00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:12.520
one before the Help
Page redesign, that's

31
00:01:12.520 --> 00:01:15.780
the order it's going to
appear in up here at the top,

32
00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:18.310
Now, if you're working with
one client on several projects,

33
00:01:18.310 --> 00:01:21.060
one handy dandy
little tip is to group

34
00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:23.235
the projects using
a common prefix,

35
00:01:23.235 --> 00:01:25.712
So you can see we've
got the Acme Corp here

36
00:01:25.712 --> 00:01:27.170
at the beginning
of these projects,

37
00:01:27.170 --> 00:01:30.110
We've used Basecamp, the
name of our product here,

38
00:01:30.110 --> 00:01:32.210
at the front of these just
to group those together

39
00:01:32.210 --> 00:01:34.669
and make them a little
bit easier to find,

40
00:01:34.669 --> 00:01:36.210
So the next step I
want to talk about

41
00:01:36.210 --> 00:01:38.690
is when you invite
people to your account,

42
00:01:38.690 --> 00:01:41.950
It's important to know which
people and projects they'll be

43
00:01:41.950 --> 00:01:42.500
able to see,

44
00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:45.810
So we've got our recently active
people listed here at the top,

45
00:01:45.810 --> 00:01:47.930
A couple of people to
remember-- the account owner

46
00:01:47.930 --> 00:01:50.305
is going to be able to see
every project and every person

47
00:01:50.305 --> 00:01:51.320
in the account,

48
00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:53.610
In ours, Merissa is
the account owner here,

49
00:01:53.610 --> 00:01:56.550
so she's able to see
everything and everyone,

50
00:01:56.550 --> 00:01:58.660
Admins can see every
user in their account

51
00:01:58.660 --> 00:02:01.640
but can only see projects
they've been invited to,

52
00:02:01.640 --> 00:02:03.560
For instance, Joan
here is an admin

53
00:02:03.560 --> 00:02:05.730
so she'll be able
to see everyone that

54
00:02:05.730 --> 00:02:08.180
is a part of the account,
but she can still

55
00:02:08.180 --> 00:02:10.630
only see the projects that
she's part of, like this,

56
00:02:10.630 --> 00:02:13.550
Ultimately, [INAUDIBLE] here,
the customer ideas project,

57
00:02:13.550 --> 00:02:14.710
that kind of thing,

58
00:02:14.710 --> 00:02:18.470
Non-admin users only see the
projects they've been added to,

59
00:02:18.470 --> 00:02:20.980
and they can only see people
that they share a project with,

60
00:02:20.980 --> 00:02:22.830
So let's invite
someone to the account

61
00:02:22.830 --> 00:02:26.342
and chat a bit more about
those Basecamp superpowers,

62
00:02:26.342 --> 00:02:28.800
To add someone, we're just
going to click on the Add Person

63
00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:30.610
right here and we'll
type their name,

64
00:02:30.610 --> 00:02:32.300
We've got a designer
that we need

65
00:02:32.300 --> 00:02:34.730
to get added so we'll have her,

66
00:02:38.470 --> 00:02:41.680
The next step is which projects
they can have access to,

67
00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:45.650
so in this one we're just going
to add her to these two right

68
00:02:45.650 --> 00:02:48.360
here,

69
00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:49.975
We'll add her to the
general calender,

70
00:02:49.975 --> 00:02:51.350
and then here's
those superpowers

71
00:02:51.350 --> 00:02:52.474
that we were talking about,

72
00:02:52.474 --> 00:02:55.600
So the two big ones that
anybody can have is the

73
00:02:55.600 --> 00:02:57.240
can create new
projects, which sounds

74
00:02:57.240 --> 00:02:59.020
exactly what the name says,

75
00:02:59.020 --> 00:03:01.790
They'll be able to create
new projects in your account,

76
00:03:01.790 --> 00:03:03.660
They can also be
an administrator

77
00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:04.710
if you allow them to be,

78
00:03:04.710 --> 00:03:09.290
So admins are people that
are able to create projects,

79
00:03:09.290 --> 00:03:11.260
They can remove
anyone from a project,

80
00:03:11.260 --> 00:03:13.820
they can remove users from
your Basecamp account,

81
00:03:13.820 --> 00:03:16.390
and they can give that
admin power to other people,

82
00:03:16.390 --> 00:03:19.050
We definitely recommend only
granting admin powers to people

83
00:03:19.050 --> 00:03:20.190
that you really trust,

84
00:03:20.190 --> 00:03:22.570
With Gina here, she doesn't
need that admin status

85
00:03:22.570 --> 00:03:24.590
so we won't add that one,

86
00:03:24.590 --> 00:03:26.077
The last one that
we'll see is one

87
00:03:26.077 --> 00:03:28.410
that I'm not able to see since
I'm not the account owner

88
00:03:28.410 --> 00:03:30.620
but it's called the
billing liaison,

89
00:03:30.620 --> 00:03:32.757
The billing liaison can
upgrade and downgrade

90
00:03:32.757 --> 00:03:34.840
your account plan, they
can update the credit card

91
00:03:34.840 --> 00:03:36.520
on file-- basically,
they're going

92
00:03:36.520 --> 00:03:39.080
to be able to handle that
billing aspect of your account,

93
00:03:39.080 --> 00:03:41.970
Billing liaisons do not
automatically have admin power,

94
00:03:41.970 --> 00:03:44.980
so you would be able to
separate those out if you need,

95
00:03:44.980 --> 00:03:47.080
We'll send this
invite out and then

96
00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:49.230
she'll be added to that project,

97
00:03:49.230 --> 00:03:51.040
Now, one handy tip with
this Everyone page,

98
00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:53.248
Notice that you're seeing
a couple of email addresses

99
00:03:53.248 --> 00:03:55.664
pop up like this and then
some of us have names,

100
00:03:55.664 --> 00:03:57.080
If you're seeing
a name like this,

101
00:03:57.080 --> 00:03:58.350
like we're seeing
with Merissa here,

102
00:03:58.350 --> 00:04:00.260
that means she's already
accepted the invite,

103
00:04:00.260 --> 00:04:03.590
she's on the account already
and enable to login to Basecamp,

104
00:04:03.590 --> 00:04:06.114
Until Gina accepts
her email invite

105
00:04:06.114 --> 00:04:08.030
she'll show us that email
address right there,

106
00:04:08.030 --> 00:04:10.080
so it's a handy way to
see which people haven't

107
00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:11.800
accepted that invite yet,

108
00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:14.130
If she didn't get the
email, you can always

109
00:04:14.130 --> 00:04:16.760
resend it by clicking this
resend the email link here,

110
00:04:16.760 --> 00:04:22.019
or just copy and paste this URL
here and pass it over to her,

111
00:04:22.019 --> 00:04:24.130
Back on the Everyone
page, we've got a section

112
00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:26.380
below the people that's
called Companies,

113
00:04:26.380 --> 00:04:28.040
Now companies and
groups are ways

114
00:04:28.040 --> 00:04:29.970
that you'll be able
to easily organize

115
00:04:29.970 --> 00:04:32.312
everybody in your account,

116
00:04:32.312 --> 00:04:34.770
We've got one company set up
here called Basecamp, and then

117
00:04:34.770 --> 00:04:36.860
a couple of different
groups under that,

118
00:04:36.860 --> 00:04:39.780
To create a new company, we'll
just click on Make a Company,

119
00:04:39.780 --> 00:04:43.196
and we'll give it
a name like that,

120
00:04:43.196 --> 00:04:45.320
and then we'll just start
adding some people to it,

121
00:04:45.320 --> 00:04:47.980
So for instance, in
this one maybe Joan

122
00:04:47.980 --> 00:04:51.310
is part of this company,
Emily's part of this company,

123
00:04:51.310 --> 00:04:52.560
and then Ann,

124
00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:53.530
Like that,

125
00:04:53.530 --> 00:04:55.730
After we get them added
we'll create the company,

126
00:04:55.730 --> 00:04:57.410
and they're right there,

127
00:04:57.410 --> 00:05:01.510
Now, say for instance, there was
a HR group inside that company,

128
00:05:01.510 --> 00:05:05.370
We'll put HR and we'll
add Emily and Joan to that

129
00:05:05.370 --> 00:05:08.640
since they're part of the
HR company for Acme Corp,

130
00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:10.140
Now, you're probably
asking yourself

131
00:05:10.140 --> 00:05:11.374
where these come in handy,

132
00:05:11.374 --> 00:05:13.290
There's going to a couple
of different places,

133
00:05:13.290 --> 00:05:18.310
Whenever you add a
new project, you'll

134
00:05:18.310 --> 00:05:22.280
be able to easily add them as
part of your team or the client

135
00:05:22.280 --> 00:05:24.660
without having to type
out each individual name,

136
00:05:24.660 --> 00:05:26.460
So for this one
we'll say that we're

137
00:05:26.460 --> 00:05:32.300
working on a website design and
that we're working with them,

138
00:05:32.300 --> 00:05:35.630
So I'm just typing Acme, and
then that auto fills like that

139
00:05:35.630 --> 00:05:37.476
and we can start the project,

140
00:05:37.476 --> 00:05:39.350
Now, the other big places
this comes in handy

141
00:05:39.350 --> 00:05:42.010
is when you are sending
out email notifications,

142
00:05:42.010 --> 00:05:45.600
So we'll start the
first discussion here,

143
00:05:45.600 --> 00:05:52.570
we'll put a kickoff message
up, and notice down here

144
00:05:52.570 --> 00:05:55.580
I've this option to choose which
people should get an email,

145
00:05:55.580 --> 00:05:58.230
When I click on that I
can choose that Acme Corp

146
00:05:58.230 --> 00:06:01.610
company over on the right to
automatically add those three

147
00:06:01.610 --> 00:06:05.490
people that we added to it, or
I can just pick that HR group

148
00:06:05.490 --> 00:06:07.890
and have only Joan and
Emily receive those email

149
00:06:07.890 --> 00:06:09.110
notifications,

150
00:06:09.110 --> 00:06:12.090
And that's how you make the most
of the companies and groups,

151
00:06:12.090 --> 00:06:13.756
So let's take a peek
at the Project page

152
00:06:13.756 --> 00:06:16.500
and I'll show you some tips
to best organize your to-dos,

153
00:06:16.500 --> 00:06:19.040
We're just going to go into
this Support Help Page Redesign

154
00:06:19.040 --> 00:06:20.804
project that we've got here,

155
00:06:20.804 --> 00:06:22.720
Now, to-dos can simply
be dragged in any order

156
00:06:22.720 --> 00:06:23.500
that you want,

157
00:06:23.500 --> 00:06:24.520
You've probably
already figured that

158
00:06:24.520 --> 00:06:26.010
out when you were
using Basecamp,

159
00:06:26.010 --> 00:06:27.930
but one of the handy
things that we do

160
00:06:27.930 --> 00:06:30.360
is drag the most
important ones to the top,

161
00:06:30.360 --> 00:06:33.244
So if I think this Live Classes
needs to be done first--

162
00:06:33.244 --> 00:06:34.910
it has the most
priority for something--

163
00:06:34.910 --> 00:06:37.370
I'm going to just drag and drop
that to the top of the list

164
00:06:37.370 --> 00:06:38.340
here,

165
00:06:38.340 --> 00:06:40.810
Now, one thing you can also
do to give it a visual kick

166
00:06:40.810 --> 00:06:43.280
is to use something
called emoji,

167
00:06:43.280 --> 00:06:45.752
Head over to emoji hyphen
cheat hyphen sheet dot com,

168
00:06:45.752 --> 00:06:48.160
and this is going to show
you all the different emojis

169
00:06:48.160 --> 00:06:49.890
that Basecamp can use,

170
00:06:49.890 --> 00:06:52.800
Now when it comes to priorities,
one of the easy things to do

171
00:06:52.800 --> 00:06:55.270
is use the symbol section
down here-- these numbers

172
00:06:55.270 --> 00:06:57.130
one through five--
to indicate which

173
00:06:57.130 --> 00:06:58.850
ones have different priorities,

174
00:06:58.850 --> 00:07:03.010
So I'm going to grab this
symbol for the emoji one,

175
00:07:03.010 --> 00:07:05.590
and then I'm going to edit
this to-do right here,

176
00:07:05.590 --> 00:07:08.820
paste that in, and that
changes just like that,

177
00:07:08.820 --> 00:07:11.420
Now, if these more videos are
maybe more of a level three

178
00:07:11.420 --> 00:07:15.660
priority we can do three there,
and the Basecamp case study

179
00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:18.345
will say that's a
level three as well,

180
00:07:18.345 --> 00:07:20.220
When a to-do item has
a few little tasks that

181
00:07:20.220 --> 00:07:22.410
need to be completed in
order to check it off,

182
00:07:22.410 --> 00:07:24.750
you could always leave
those as a comment

183
00:07:24.750 --> 00:07:25.910
on the original to-do,

184
00:07:25.910 --> 00:07:28.050
So for instance, with
these Live Classes

185
00:07:28.050 --> 00:07:30.210
here, some of the things
that [? Kristen's ?]

186
00:07:30.210 --> 00:07:36.560
going to need to do is
draft up some scripts,

187
00:07:36.560 --> 00:07:47.019
record a trial run, and then set
up the class registration site,

188
00:07:47.019 --> 00:07:48.560
We'll add that
comment there and then

189
00:07:48.560 --> 00:07:51.270
[? Kristen ?] can go through
those many to-dos whatever

190
00:07:51.270 --> 00:07:55.010
she is getting ready to tackle
this live classes to-do,

191
00:07:55.010 --> 00:07:57.510
Now, the cool thing with emoji
is that Basecamp supports it

192
00:07:57.510 --> 00:07:58.070
anywhere,

193
00:07:58.070 --> 00:08:00.100
So if you just want
to give somebody

194
00:08:00.100 --> 00:08:04.550
a thumbs up, maybe say you
understand what they were

195
00:08:04.550 --> 00:08:06.670
talking about or anything
like that, we'll go here

196
00:08:06.670 --> 00:08:11.735
and we'll say something like
plus 1 for the thumbs up emoji,

197
00:08:11.735 --> 00:08:17.110
and we'll say, thanks, Gina,
and add the comment like that,

198
00:08:17.110 --> 00:08:20.435
Notice that thumbs up emoji
appears inside of the comment,

199
00:08:20.435 --> 00:08:22.580
so anywhere you can
type text you'll

200
00:08:22.580 --> 00:08:25.220
be able to add those
emojis inside Basecamp,

201
00:08:25.220 --> 00:08:26.600
So here's something
a little fun,

202
00:08:26.600 --> 00:08:28.474
How about some
keyboard shortcuts?

203
00:08:28.474 --> 00:08:29.890
There are a few
keyboard shortcuts

204
00:08:29.890 --> 00:08:32.380
to help you navigate through
the different areas of Basecamp,

205
00:08:32.380 --> 00:08:34.070
and by areas that's
these areas up here,

206
00:08:34.070 --> 00:08:37.750
The Projects, the Calendar,
everything, so on and so forth,

207
00:08:37.750 --> 00:08:40.049
So we're going to hit the
letter G and the number 1,

208
00:08:40.049 --> 00:08:42.740
That takes us to the
Project page just like this,

209
00:08:42.740 --> 00:08:46.510
G+2 takes us to the Calendar,
G+3 takes us to Everything,

210
00:08:46.510 --> 00:08:51.130
G+4 is the Progress page, G+5
is Everyone, and then G+6,

211
00:08:51.130 --> 00:08:54.170
you guessed it, takes
me over to my Me page,

212
00:08:54.170 --> 00:08:56.310
Now, if I want to get
over to this job area--

213
00:08:56.310 --> 00:08:58.450
this jump or search
or whatever-- then you

214
00:08:58.450 --> 00:09:01.720
can use the keyboard shortcut
G+F, It puts you right there,

215
00:09:01.720 --> 00:09:03.940
so I could start typing
in Merissa's name

216
00:09:03.940 --> 00:09:06.190
and go to her page without
ever having to actually use

217
00:09:06.190 --> 00:09:08.216
my mouse for any of that,

218
00:09:08.216 --> 00:09:09.590
Another thing
that's really handy

219
00:09:09.590 --> 00:09:11.210
if you're on a
long page like this

220
00:09:11.210 --> 00:09:13.086
if you want to get to
the very bottom of it--

221
00:09:13.086 --> 00:09:15.376
we're going to double click
down here on the beige area

222
00:09:15.376 --> 00:09:17.940
and that takes us to the bottom
of any page inside Basecamp,

223
00:09:17.940 --> 00:09:19.740
so we could immediately
get to see those

224
00:09:19.740 --> 00:09:21.480
files that Merissa shared,

225
00:09:21.480 --> 00:09:24.262
When I see the
file that I need, I

226
00:09:24.262 --> 00:09:25.970
can always double
click in the top corner

227
00:09:25.970 --> 00:09:26.890
to get back to the top,

228
00:09:26.890 --> 00:09:28.806
And this is going to
work in all four corners,

229
00:09:28.806 --> 00:09:31.470
so we'll double click down
here in the right side

230
00:09:31.470 --> 00:09:34.630
and then we can do that again
in the upper right side as well,

231
00:09:34.630 --> 00:09:35.574
Pretty cool, right?

232
00:09:35.574 --> 00:09:36.990
The next tip I'm
going to touch on

233
00:09:36.990 --> 00:09:38.980
is how to take your
Basecamp calendar

234
00:09:38.980 --> 00:09:41.550
and bring them over into some
of the other calendar apps

235
00:09:41.550 --> 00:09:42.720
that you're using,

236
00:09:42.720 --> 00:09:44.480
So on the Calendar
page we're going

237
00:09:44.480 --> 00:09:47.541
to click Subscribe to iCal in
the lower left corner here,

238
00:09:47.541 --> 00:09:50.040
That's going to give us a list
of all of the iCalendar feeds

239
00:09:50.040 --> 00:09:51.180
that Basecamp offers,

240
00:09:51.180 --> 00:09:53.180
